# kiwi-proxy 9proxy provider — 9proxy's own Linux client (daemon and CLI), from
# 9proxy's download server at build time (it is not redistributed here). Built by
# `kiwi-proxy module setup 9proxy` as kiwi-proxy/9proxy:latest.
#
# Fedora and the RPM, as the user's own 9proxy-pod runs it. The daemon serves
# ports 60000-60009, one residential IP each, on this container's address on the
# providers bridge, where only kiwi-proxy's gateways reach them.
FROM registry.fedoraproject.org/fedora:latest
ARG NINEPROXY_RPM=https://static.9proxy-cdn.net/download/latest/linux/9proxy-linux-redhat-amd64.rpm
RUN dnf -y -q install "$NINEPROXY_RPM" \
 && dnf clean all \
 && test -x /usr/bin/9proxy
# The ports listen on the container's own address (the entrypoint writes it into
# the config from KF_9PROXY_IP): 9proxy takes no 0.0.0.0, and the gateway is
# another container.
RUN grep -q '"default_ip_format"' /etc/9proxy-config.json
COPY entrypoint.sh /usr/local/bin/kf-9proxy
RUN chmod 755 /usr/local/bin/kf-9proxy
ENTRYPOINT ["/usr/local/bin/kf-9proxy"]
